  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Full Derecognition — Risks and Rewards Substantially Transferred" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Continued Recognition — Risks and Rewards Substantially Retained" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. The Control Test — the Fallback for Ambiguous Cases" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Continuing Involvement Accounting" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Common Practical Examples" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — a Factoring Arrangement Qualifying for Derecognition" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Continuing Involvement Under a Retained Guarantee" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IFRS 9" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Chinese GAAP (ASBE / CAS) · 金融资产转移 · The risks-and-rewards derecognition test, converged with IFRS 9 · RMB examples</div></div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Determining when a financial asset should come off the Balance Sheet</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 23 governs the DERECOGNITION of FINANCIAL assets — DETERMINING WHEN a TRANSFERRED financial ASSET should be REMOVED from the TRANSFEROR'S Balance SHEET, RATHER than CONTINUING to be RECOGNISED (WHOLLY or PARTIALLY). This STANDARD works ALONGSIDE ASBE No. 22 (CLASSIFICATION and measurement) to FORM the COMPLETE financial ASSET accounting FRAMEWORK, CLOSELY converged with IFRS 9'S own DERECOGNITION model internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Sales, factoring, securitisation, and similar transfer arrangements</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to TRANSACTIONS in WHICH an ENTERPRISE TRANSFERS a FINANCIAL asset (or a PART of one) to ANOTHER party — COVERING outright SALES, FACTORING of RECEIVABLES, SECURITISATION arrangements, and REPURCHASE (repo) TRANSACTIONS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Full Derecognition — Risks and Rewards Substantially Transferred</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The primary test for derecognition</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">WHERE an ENTERPRISE TRANSFERS SUBSTANTIALLY ALL the RISKS and REWARDS of OWNERSHIP of a FINANCIAL asset, the ASSET is DERECOGNISED IN FULL, WITH the DIFFERENCE between the CARRYING amount and the CONSIDERATION received RECOGNISED as a GAIN or LOSS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Continued Recognition — Risks and Rewards Substantially Retained</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">No derecognition, a corresponding liability instead</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">WHERE an ENTERPRISE RETAINS SUBSTANTIALLY ALL the RISKS and REWARDS of OWNERSHIP (e.g. a SALE with a REPURCHASE agreement at a FIXED price), the ASSET CONTINUES to be RECOGNISED IN FULL, WITH the CONSIDERATION received RECOGNISED as a FINANCIAL liability, RATHER than a SALE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>The Control Test — the Fallback for Ambiguous Cases</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Applied where risks and rewards are neither clearly transferred nor retained</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">WHERE it is NOT clear WHETHER SUBSTANTIALLY all RISKS and REWARDS have been TRANSFERRED or RETAINED, the ENTERPRISE assesses WHETHER it has RETAINED CONTROL of the ASSET — IF control is RETAINED, the ASSET continues to be RECOGNISED to the EXTENT of the ENTERPRISE'S continuing INVOLVEMENT (Section 6); IF control PASSES to the TRANSFEREE, the ASSET is DERECOGNISED.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Continuing Involvement Accounting</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognising an asset and liability limited to the retained exposure</div><div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">WHERE the ENTERPRISE retains a LIMITED, ONGOING exposure to the TRANSFERRED asset (e.g. a GUARANTEE, or a RETAINED subordinated INTEREST), it CONTINUES to RECOGNISE the ASSET (and a CORRESPONDING liability) ONLY to the EXTENT of its CONTINUING involvement — RATHER than either FULL derecognition or FULL continued RECOGNITION.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Common Practical Examples</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Recurring transfer arrangements in Chinese practice</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Factoring of trade receivables (with or without recourse)</span><span>Asset securitisation (bundling receivables into tradable securities)</span><span>Repurchase (repo) agreements</span><span>Discounting of notes receivable</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — a Factoring Arrangement Qualifying for Derecognition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A genuine, non-recourse sale of receivables</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Non-recourse factoring of trade receivables</div><div class="wk-body">A company factors RMB 50,000,000 of trade receivables to a bank on a genuinely NON-RECOURSE basis, receiving RMB 47,000,000 cash, with the bank bearing all credit risk and no ongoing involvement retained by the company.</div><div class="wk-answer">Since SUBSTANTIALLY all RISKS and REWARDS are TRANSFERRED, the company DERECOGNISES the RMB 50,000,000 receivable IN FULL, recognising a LOSS on transfer of RMB 50,000,000 − RMB 47,000,000 = <strong>RMB 3,000,000</strong>.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Continuing Involvement Under a Retained Guarantee</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Partial derecognition, limited to the retained exposure</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Factoring with a partial credit guarantee</div><div class="wk-body">A company factors RMB 30,000,000 of receivables, but retains a guarantee covering the first RMB 3,000,000 of any credit losses (its maximum possible exposure).</div><div class="wk-answer">The company CONTINUES to recognise an ASSET (and a CORRESPONDING liability) of <strong>RMB 3,000,000</strong> — LIMITED to its CONTINUING involvement — DERECOGNISING the REMAINING RMB 27,000,000 of receivables, since it has NO further EXPOSURE beyond the GUARANTEE.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 23 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature and carrying amount of transferred financial assets not qualifying for full derecognition</span><span>Nature and extent of any continuing involvement retained</span><span>Gain or loss recognised on transfers qualifying for full derecognition</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether substantially all risks and rewards have been transferred, retained, or shared</span><span>Whether control has passed where the risks-and-rewards test is inconclusive</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of any retained continuing involvement asset or liability</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 9</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 23 vs IFRS 9's derecognition provisions</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 23</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 9</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Risks-and-rewards primary test</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Control test fallback</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED standard — the DERECOGNITION logic MIRRORS IFRS 9'S own APPROACH closely.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every transfer event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Full derecognition</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Gain/loss recognised on transfer</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Continuing involvement</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Asset and liability limited to the retained exposure</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 22</span><span>Recognition and Measurement of Financial Instruments — supplies the classification framework this Standard's derecognition provisions apply to</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Derecognition</div><div class="glossary-def">The removal of a previously recognised financial asset from an entity's Balance Sheet.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Continuing involvement</div><div class="glossary-def">A retained exposure to a transferred financial asset (such as a guarantee), requiring partial continued recognition limited to that exposure.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) <span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) <span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) <span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe23 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
